hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24070","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Ibn Jurayj, informed to me Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, that a man of the Ansar narrated to him: He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in a gathering, and whispered to him, seeking his permission to kill a man of the hypocrites. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke aloud and said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah? The Ansari said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but there is no testimony for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does he not testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but there is no testimony for him. Does he not pray? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but there is no prayer for him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those are the ones Allah has forbidden me from."
"24071","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Ubaydullah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from Abdullah ibn Adi al-Ansari, he narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was sitting, a man came to him, meaning seeking his permission, whispering to him privately. And he mentioned its meaning."
